From 3cafa9be68140ba06f7c91a6caf2b95a8083dcce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:44:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Shorten the leave and release confirms

The armed line of Leave the campaign (the desk and the hub's registry)
and of Release from the circle (the Lightkeeper's copy of the sheet) was
a paragraph (issue #62). It is now one short sentence, "Press again to
leave <campaign>." or "Press again to release <name>.", and the armed
button reads Leave or Release (decision 4). What goes with the
investigator, which decision 1 of fix round 4 asks the confirm to say,
is behind an "i" beside the line, "What leaving does" or "What release
does": coming back free, the votes, relationships and report dropped,
the resources lowered on a sealed circle, and any Train die lost.

ConfirmAction takes armedInfo, laid in the armed hint's row inside the
confirm, so pressing the "i" leaves it armed. DESIGN.md and FAQ.md say
so.

Checked: vite build; in Chromium at 390x844, 820x1180 and 1366x768 the
desk's Leave, the hub's registry Leave and the Lightkeeper's Release arm
with the short line, the "i" opens its slip on screen (above the button
at the foot of a sheet, under the row on the hub), the button stays
armed, no sideways scroll and no page errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETKqHLvkfH9k99JTnJzzKA
